course: dictionary
lesson: 10556
title: Unbroken: whole, or never stopping
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the clues around them show you which one the writer means. Unbroken can mean not damaged, without a gap, or a record that nobody has beaten. «Many philosophers say you are the same person because of a long unbroken chain.» A chain with no breaks links everything together, so unbroken here means continuous, with nothing missing.
explain: «Apple pips usually pass out unbroken» tells you the pip comes out still whole, not cracked. The words around unbroken point to not damaged, so that is the meaning to choose here.
explain: To check, swap in your meaning and read the sentence again. «A whole swallowed pip usually passes out whole» still makes sense, so you have it right. If the swap does not fit, try another meaning.
fact: Unbroken means not broken or damaged, like an unbroken egg.
fact: Unbroken also means without a stop or gap, like an unbroken line.
fact: An unbroken record is one that has not been beaten yet.
fact: An unbroken horse has not been trained to carry a rider.
fact: Phrases to know: unbroken silence, unbroken chain, unbroken record, unbroken line.
exercise: «The egg was still unbroken after it fell off the table.» What does unbroken mean? | Very cold | Cracked into small pieces | *Not broken or damaged | Covered in paint
exercise: «She drew an unbroken line across the page without lifting her pencil.» What does unbroken suggest? | *Continuous, with no gaps or stops | Drawn in a hurry | Wobbly and uneven | Written in red ink
exercise: The swimmer's record has stayed unbroken for ten years. What does this mean? | *No one has beaten the record yet | The record was made by a horse | The record was lost | The swimmer broke a leg
test: «He kept an unbroken silence all through the long meeting.» What does unbroken silence mean? | Loud shouting | Quiet music playing softly | *Silence with no stops or gaps | A broken promise
test: «The wild horse was unbroken, and no rider had ever sat on its back.» What does unbroken mean for a horse? | *Not yet trained to carry a rider | Trained to jump fences | Very fast and strong | Carrying heavy loads
exam: Which meaning of unbroken fits «a long unbroken chain of days with no missed practice»? | Not broken or damaged | Not yet beaten | *Continuous, without any gaps | Not trained to carry a rider
